    ; ★★★ A VIEW OF A TEMPORARY STRING DOES NOT SURVIVE THE ROUTINE THAT MADE IT.
    ; `b.to_string()` constructs its String on the CALLER page — the calling
    ; routine's own region — so `slice_of(b.to_string())` RETURNED or STORED is a
    ; view into memory that dies with the return (measured: 90 of 90 bytes wrong
    ; after the next allocations; a returned String VALUE survives, a slice of
    ; it does not — §3.5ji). This copies the bytes onto `host` first.
